-- 12 note LE-pinned format, §9.1 pins no byte order — FIXED, doc-only:
--    `schemes.state_sha` and `schemes.fid` spell LE explicitly in every written
--    manifest, and segment.rs now carries an explicit BYTE ORDER paragraph
--    (all fixed-width integers little-endian; varints LEB128; canon-v1 payloads
--    keep their own big-endian order). NOT MEASURED: an actual big-endian run.
-- 13 note POSITIVE — the nondeterminism hunt found nothing, across four
--    independent processes with zero exclusions — RECORDED. E7 is structural,
--    not accidental. This round added two more processes (f3 path-spelling,
--    f4 rebuild), so the property now has six independent confirmations.
-- 20 note (≡35) the implementer's «141 NOT MEASURED / preds.py absent» claim
--    is factually wrong — ACCEPTED AND THE CLAIM RETRACTED. See X2: the
--    reconciliation is exact with zero residual, and the same wrong claim was
--    repeated once inside this phase before being checked. The lesson is the
--    Evidence Rule applied to one's OWN prior sentences.
-- 26 note conflict/5 decl duplicated inline — FIXED: the converter now derives
--    the physics from `PredicateCatalog::conflict_decl()` and asserts every
--    field it depends on (MultiValued, Timeless, BoolTag, empty priority,
--    arity == CONFLICT_COLUMNS.len()), so a catalog change cannot drift past it.
-- 27 note no-op `.map(|v| v)` in verify_c1 — FIXED: deleted.
-- 28 note metrics.facts adds the in-memory conflict counter — FIXED: it uses
--    the PERSISTED `conflict` decl's live_facts, guarded by a drift gate that
--    fails if in-memory and on-disk disagree. VERIFIED on the real base: the
--    manifest's own Σ live_facts equals the reported metrics.facts exactly.
-- 33 note (≡2) — see 2.
-- 34 note bloom + zone map are write-only, 11,239,384 B unexercised —
--    REJECTED AS A STAGE-1 DEFECT, with the cost recorded (1.651% of the
--    store). Grounds the reviewer can check: (a) F1 pre-registers exactly this
--    («The reader does not NEED bloom/zone — full-scan verification; they are
--    the §3.2 conventions carried into the format»), so this is a registered
--    property, not a discovery; (b) the structures are NOT untested — the
--    reviewer's own suggested test already exists at the encoder level:
--    `bloom_has_no_false_negatives_and_still_rejects_absent_keys`
--    (convert/segment.rs) and `zone_map_min_max_bound_the_leading_column`
--    (convert/segment.rs) assert precisely «every Id-typed leading key present
--    is accepted by its own bloom» and «every key falls inside the zone-map
--    bounds»; (c) their probe and parameter rules are now in
--    `schemes.bloom`, so a stage-2 reader can consume them without the
--    converter source. Building the PROBE path is stage 2's read path, which is
--    where a probe can be measured against a real query. Writing them now is
--    what makes the store usable then without a re-encode.
-- 35 note (≡20) — see 20.

